# Git and IDE
**/.git
**/.github
**/.gitignore
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.classpath
**/.dockerignore
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.next
**/.cache
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm

# Dependencies (installed in container)
**/node_modules
**/.npm
**/npm-debug.log

# Build outputs (rebuilt in container)
**/build
**/dist
./frontend/dist
./frontend/dist/*

# Documentation and tests (not needed in production)
docs/
tests/
test-results/
**/*.md
LICENSE
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Local development files
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.yml
!config/*.yml
!backend/config/*.yml
# Rubik's Cube course content — must reach the image if authored (mirrors the
# .gitignore negation); courseCatalog.mjs degrades gracefully when absent.
!backend/src/3_applications/school/rubiksCube/course.yml
secrets.dev.yaml
values.dev.yaml
**/charts
**/docker-compose*
# Compose's modern filenames only. This used to be `**/compose*`, which is a
# prefix glob over EVERY path segment, not just compose files: it silently
# dropped `composerCardTiming.js` out of the build context while leaving
# `ComposerCard.jsx` (capital C) in, so the image failed to build on an import
# that resolves fine in the repo. Any lowercase compose-prefixed source file
# would hit the same trap.
**/compose.yml
**/compose.yaml
**/compose.*.yml
**/compose.*.yaml
**/obj

# Data and logs (mounted at runtime)
./data
./data/*
logs/
*.log

# Dev tools
playwright.config.js
jest.config.js
babel.config.js
nodemon.json
dev
sandbox.sh
Dockerfile.dev
docker-compose.dev.yml

# Extensions (separate build)
_extensions/
_extentions/
